    "thumbnail_url": "https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8573595-S.jpg",
    "details": {
      "description": {
        "type": "/type/text",
        "value": "\"On a May afternoon in 1943, an American military plane crashed into the Pacific Ocean and disappeared, leaving only a spray of debris and a slick of oil, gasoline, and blood. Then, on the ocean surface, a face appeared. It was that of a young lieutenant, the plane's bombardier, who was struggling to a life raft and pulling himself aboard. So began one of the most extraordinary sagas of the Second World War. The lieutenant's name was Louis Zamperini.\"--Jacket."
      },
      "notes": {
        "type": "/type/text",
        "value": "\"Adapted for young adults.\"\r\n\r\nOriginal version published: New York : Random House, ©2010.\r\n\r\nIncludes index.\r\n\r\nIncludes bibliographical references and index.\r\n\r\nAccelerated Reader 6.4."
      },
